 prereq:["conscience","synderesis","scrupulosity-c","vincible-ignorance","prudence","natural-law"],
 recall:[
  ["t6l2","Which ignorance excuses and which does not?","Antecedent, invincible ignorance causes the involuntary and excuses; affected or negligent (vincible) ignorance does not (q.6 a.8)."],
  ["t6","What is synderesis?","The natural habit of the first principles of practical reason ('good is to be done, evil avoided'); it cannot err in its principles."],
  ["t6l3","Why can a good intention not justify an intrinsically evil act?","Because the object gives the first moral species; a good end cannot heal an evil object (q.18 aa.2, 6; VS 80)."],
  ["p4","What is scrupulosity?","A form of obsessive-compulsive presentation in which a person is tormented by unfounded fears of sin or moral wrongdoing, often with compulsive reassurance-seeking or confession."]],
